Which target each test measured
-------------------------------
Test 1 (the endpoint) always hits PRODUCTION: the spec names
`https://forgotten-mistory.web.app/api/tts` absolutely, because `/api/tts` is a
Cloud Function behind a Hosting rewrite and does not exist in a static export.
So this pass is a live pass against the function deployed in this task — the
same request that returned `502 {"error":"tts_upstream_failed","status":401}`
in `02-tests-failing.log` half an hour earlier.

Test 2 (the label) follows `PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL`, and was run here against the
static export built from this branch's working tree, because the label is a
client change and Hosting has not been redeployed yet — the pipeline
(`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) consolidates this branch into `main` and
deploys within ten minutes of the push. Against the live origin it still fails
until that deploy lands, exactly as it did in `02-tests-failing.log`; the
function half is already live.

Paid calls in this run: one, the spec's own 5-character `{"text":"probe"}`.

